## STATE MANAGEMENT RULES (Feature A)
# NEVER put API response data in Zustand — TanStack Query cache only
# queryKey arrays in useQuery MUST match queryClient.invalidateQueries exactly
# All Zustand stores use immer middleware — no spread operators in set()
# useMutation retry: 0 always — mutations are not idempotent
# select() in useQuery transforms data once — components receive clean types
# placeholderData: keepPreviousData on all paginated/filtered queries


## ANIMATION RULES (Feature B)
# Framer Motion: ONLY animate transform and opacity — never width/height/layout
# AnimatePresence must have mode="wait" and initial={false} always
# motion.div key prop must change when animated content changes
# useReducedMotion() MUST be checked in all animated components
# Lottie loop=false for success/completion animations
# All transition durations between 0.25s and 0.5s — never slower


## EMAIL / INVITATION RULES (Feature C)
# Raw invite tokens NEVER stored in DB — SHA-256 hash only
# Raw tokens NEVER appear in structlog calls (security)
# Email sending ALWAYS via Celery task — HTTP endpoint never calls SMTP directly
# HTML email templates use table layout only — no flex, no grid (Outlook)
# Jinja2 autoescape ALWAYS enabled for email templates
# resend() MUST revoke old token before issuing new token
# validate token endpoint is public but has rate limiting
